  "text": "BOARD OF ELECTIONS | Caswell County | NC\ntop of page\nNOTICE for Thursday, 2/5:\nCounty offices will open at 11am Thursday due to road conditions.\nDOCUMENT CENTER\nCALENDAR\nGOVERNMENT\nOPEN BIDS\nCOMMISSIONER MINUTES ARCHIVE\nDEPARTMENTS\nRESIDENTS\nBUSINESS\nVISITORS\nMore\nUse tab to navigate through the menu items.\nElections\nBOARD OF\nQUICK\nINFO\nIt is recommended you use the NCSBE Registration check tool to determine your correct ballot for the 2026 General Election.\nClick here for that info\nCONTACT\nRobert Webb - Director\nMailing Address: PO Box 698\nPhysical Location: 140 Main Street, Yanceyville, NC 27379\nPhone: (336) 694-4010 Fax: (336) 694-9924\nE-mail:\n[email protected]\nHours of Operation: 8:00 am \u2013 12:30 pm & 1:30 pm \u2013 5:00 pm M-F\nRESPONSIBILITIES\nMaintain current and accurate voter files, voter registration, educate the voting public, providing the best possible services and conduct efficient, fair, honest and impartial elections. Secure elections for all.\nMEMBERS\nYvonne D. Saul, Chair\nLarry Cowan, Secretary\n\u200b\nDora Ward,Member\nElwood Dodson,Member\nLouise Baldwin, Member\u200b\nMEETINGS\nRegular Meetings are the Third Tuesday of Each Month 5:00 pm at the Board of Elections office (unless otherwise posted-scroll down to Agenda section below for confirmation)\nDETAILS & FORMS\nOur Goal\nWelcome to the official website for the Caswell County Board of Elections. Our office is committed to maintaining current and accurate voter files, maximizing voter registration and voter turnout efforts, educating the voting public, providing the best possible services and conducting efficient, fair, honest and impartial elections at a reasonable cost to the electorate.\nWhat We Do\nThe Caswell County Board of Elections is responsible for conducting all elections held in Caswell County and locally administering State election laws. Our principal functions include:\n\u200b\nEstablishing election precincts and voting sites\nAppointing and training precinct officials\nPreparing and distributing ballots and voting equipment\nCanvassing and certifying the ballots cast in elections\nInvestigating any voting irregularities.\nWe maintain voter registration for Caswell County and provide public information on voters and elections. A major focus of the Elections Office is to maintain accuracy and security of both voter registration information and the voting process, including ensuring that each voter\u2019s records reflect that voter\u2019s correct precinct and ensuring that those who choose to vote have not been deterred or denied in any way.\nHow We Are Organized\nEach County in North Carolina has a Board of Elections. It is a five person board which is appointed every two years by the State Board of Elections. G.S.163-30, as re-recodified by this act, reads as rewritten:\"\u00a7 163-30. County boards of elections; appointments; terms of office:\n\u201cIn every county of the State there shall be a county board of elections, to consist of five persons of good moral character who are registered voters in the county in which they are to act. Members of county boards of elections shall be appointed by the State Board of Elections on the last Tuesday in June,and every two years thereafter, and their terms of office shall continue for two years from the specified date of appointment and until their successors are appointed and qualified. Four members of county boards of elections shall be appointed by the State Board on the last Tuesday in June and every two years thereafter, and their terms of office shall continue for two years from the specified date of appointment and until their successors are appointed and qualified.One member of the county boards of elections shall be appointed by the Governor to be the chair of the county board on the last Tuesday in June and every two years thereafter, and that member's term of office shall continue for two years from the specified date of appointment and until a successor is appointed and qualified.Of the appointments by the State Board, not more than two members of the county board of elections shall belong to the same political party.\u201d\nThe local political parties will submit three names to the State political party chairman. Once appointed, County Board members take an oath and begin their two year terms on the Tuesday following the third Monday in July in odd-numbered years. The Board oversees the functions of our office and hires a Director to administer all duties.\n\u200b\u200b\nElection Information\nCampaign Finance/Treasurer Training\nCampaign Finance Manual\nCampaign Finance Reporting Forms\nNCSBE Candidate Guide\n(Updated)\n2026 Soil & Water Filing Dates and Fees 6/8/26-7/6/26\n2026 Candidate Filing Packet\n(Updated)\n2026 General Notice of Election\n2026 General Election Schedule\n2026 Early Voting Buffer Zone Notice/Map\n2026 General Election Early Voting Dates\n2026 General Election Early Voting Lists\n2026 General Election Candidate List\n2026 General Election Sample Ballot Lookup\nTool\n2026 General Election Sample Ballots (all)\n2026 PRIMARY ELECTION RESULTS\nPast Election Results\nElection Day Polling Sites List (With Maps)\nCombating Misinformation\nBallot Tabulation FAQ\nUOCAVA Election Notice\nVoting Equipment\nNC Voter Photo ID Infosheet\nNC Photo ID Required to Vote Video\nNCSBE Voter ID Information Site\nQuick Links\nPolitical Signage Inquiries/Complaints\nIdentifying Official Election Office Calls to Voters\nElection Worker Requirements/Recruitment\nCheck My Voter Registration/Districts (Sample Ballots Here Also)\nAbsentee Ballot Request Form(Mail-In)\nRequest An Absentee Ballot(Online Submit)\nFind My Polling Place(NCSBE)\nNorth Carolina State Board of Elections\nRegister to Vote Today\nLocal and State Political Parties\nHow to know your vote counted\nResponse to Calls for Audit\n/Inspection of Voting Machines, etc.\n2020 General Election Recount Data\n2020 Board of Commissioner District Map\nMINUTES\n& AGENDAS\nBelow are the agendas from the most current board meetings. If you are looking for a particular year or meeting record, send email to (\n[email protected]\n)\nNOTICE\n-\nThere is limited space for in-person public attendance of meetings. When Early Voting begins we move solely to Zoom Meetings for public attendance.\n2026\nBoard of Elections\nRegular/ Post-Canvass Meeting\n11/17/2026\n05:00 PM\nView Agenda *coming soon*\n\u200b\nBoard of Elections\nElection Canvass\n11/13/2026\n11:00 AM\nView Agenda *coming soon*\n\u200b\nBoard of Elections\nPre-Canvass Meeting\n11/12/2026\n05:00 PM\nView Agenda *coming soon*\n\u200b\nBoard of Elections\nABS/Provisional Meeting\n11/10/2026\n05:00 PM\nView Agenda *coming soon*\n\u200b\nBoard of Elections\nABS/Provisional Meeting\n11/10/2026\n05:00 PM\nView Agenda *coming soon*\n\u200b\nBoard of Elections\nABS/Provisional Meeting\n11/09/2026\n05:00 PM\nView Agenda *coming soon*\n\u200b\nBoard of Elections\nElection Day Absentee Meeting\n11/03/2026\n07:30 PM\nView Agenda *coming soon*\n\u200b\nBoard of Elections\nPre-Election Meeting/ Absentee\n11/02/2026\n05:00 PM\n(Public Attendance is Zoom Only)\nView Agenda *coming soon*\n\u200b\nBoard of Elections\nAbsentee Meeting 5\n10/27/2026\n05:00 PM\n(Public Attendance is Zoom Only)\nView Agenda *coming soon*\n\u200b\nBoard of Elections\nRegular Meeting/Absentee 4\n10/20/2026\n05:00 PM\n(Public Attendance is Zoom Only)\nView Agenda *coming soon*\n\u200b\nBoard of Elections\nAbsentee Meetings 1-3\n09/29/26,10/06/26,10/13/26\n05:00 PM\n(subject to cancel if no returns recv'd)\nView Agenda\n\u200b\nBoard of Elections\nRegular Meeting\n09/15/2026\n05:00 PM\nView Agenda\n\u200b\nBoard of Elections\nRegular Meeting\n08/18/2026\n05:00 PM\nView Agenda\n\u200b\nBoard of Elections\nRegular Meeting\n07/21/2026\n05:00 PM\nView Agenda\n\u200b\nBoard of Elections\nRegular Meeting\n06/23/2026\n05:00 PM\nView Agenda\n\u200b\nBoard of Elections\nRegular Meeting\n05/19/2026\n05:00 PM\